subproblem.statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ, N ⊆ ℝ^P, x ∈ ℝ^P, ι : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^P a linear isometry with adjoint A := ι*, u : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^P and δ₁, δ₂ ∈ ℝ. Put D := B_{δ₁}(0) ⊆ ℝ^{n+1}, G(y) := x + ιy + u(y), and Z := {w ∈ ℝ^P : |A(w − x)| < δ₁ and |w − x − ιA(w − x)| < δ₂}.

Assume:
- u is C² on D;
- for every v ∈ D: u(v) ⊥ range ι, |u(v)| < δ₂/2 and G(v) ∈ N;
- whenever |v| < δ₁, |h| < δ₂, h ⊥ range ι and x + ιv + h ∈ N, then h = u(v).

Then:
(i) G is C² on D;
(ii) DG(v)a = ιa + Du(v)a for all v ∈ D and a ∈ ℝ^{n+1};
(iii) DG(v) is injective for every v ∈ D;
(iv) G is injective on D;
(v) Z is open;
(vi) D ∩ G^{-1}(K) is compact for every compact K ⊆ Z;
(vii) S ∩ Z = G(D ∩ G^{-1}(S)) for every S ⊆ N;
(viii) D ∩ G^{-1}(S) is Borel for every Borel S ⊆ ℝ^P.
